 {'title': 'Required Inspections', 'img': 'POH_8-7_inspection_periods', 'cite': '14 CFR 91.409, 14 CFR 91.403, PHAK 9-8, POH 8-7', 'code': C8,
  'bullets': ['Annual: 12 calendar months', '100-hour: for hire, instruction', 'May exceed 10 hours to shop', 'Comply with all ADs'],
  'notes': 'Annual for everyone. 100-hour if carrying people for hire or giving instruction for hire in an airplane you provide.',
  'lp': {'teach': ['Annual: no person may operate an aircraft unless it has had an annual inspection within the preceding 12 calendar months (14 CFR 91.409). Twelve calendar months runs from any day of a month to the last day of the same month the next year (PHAK 9-8).',
     '100-hour: required to carry any person (other than crew) for hire, or to give flight instruction for hire in an aircraft that person provides. It may be exceeded by not more than 10 hours to reach a place where it can be done, and the extra time counts toward the next 100 hours (14 CFR 91.409).',
     'The owner or operator is primarily responsible for keeping the aircraft airworthy, including compliance with ADs under part 39 (14 CFR 91.403). The POH says the FAA may require other inspections through ADs (POH 8-7).',
     'Note: an amendment to 91.403 and 91.409 was published November 10, 2026 and is not yet in the current text. Recheck before your checkride.']}},
